<title>USA: Heartland launches two value funds.</title>
<headline>Heartland launches two value funds.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heartland Funds said it launched two equity value funds.</p>
<p>The Heartland Mid Cap Value Fund will invest in stocks with capitalization between $500 million and $2.5 billion. Michael Berry, who came from Dreman Value Advisors in July, will manage the fund.</p>
<p>The Heartland Large Cap Value Fund, will invest in stocks with capitalization over $1 billion. James Holmes, who also came from Dreman in July, will manage the fund.</p>
<p>Heartland currently manages $2.6 billion in assets.</p>
